#{[17592186278214 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\\begin{cases}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\ne 0\\end{cases}\\hspace{2em}⟹\\hspace{2em}\\begin{cases}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\end{cases}$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\}.\n$$"]}
